  - process tomography
  - Pauli twirl
  - IBM Quantum
abstract: >-
  Code, data and notebooks of a study of two-qubit quantum teleportation through a noisy channel whose correction
  (one parametric gate per channel qubit) is learned from measurement counts only. The package simulates the
  six-qubit protocol exactly, implements the counts-only calibrators, the ceiling of any correction, process
  tomography (TOMO-9, TOMO-75) and drift tracking, and rebuilds every result of the experiments on the IBM devices
  ibm_kingston (4 October 2026) and ibm_kingston and ibm_fez (the replication of 25 October 2026) from their raw counts.
